From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:10:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 39/57] gdb: stop setting up a remote connection if the program
 has ended

A program that ended while GDB connected hit an assertion in post_create_inferior.

diff --git a/gdb/infrun.c b/gdb/infrun.c
index 148d73d6fcb..7b983990c57 100644
--- a/gdb/infrun.c
+++ b/gdb/infrun.c
@@ -3875,6 +3875,12 @@ start_remote (int from_tty)
      for an async run.  */
   wait_for_inferior (inf);
 
+  /* GDB may have resumed the program from the event it found it in,
+     e.g. a syscall stop it does not catch, and the program may have
+     ended meanwhile.  Then there is nothing to set up.  */
+  if (inferior_ptid == null_ptid)
+    error (_("The program is no longer running."));
+
   /* Now that the inferior has stopped, do any bookkeeping like
      loading shared libraries.  We want to do this before normal_stop,
      so that the displayed frame is up to date.  */
